{
  "_comment": "The deny rules every project settings file and every generated executor settings file must carry (docs/DESIGN.md sections 14 and 18.5). The first 56 are the destructive, credential-reading and human-only forms the settings template has always denied; the rest close the write and run forms of the read-only commands the category allows open (find actions, sed in place, rg and sort helper programs, jq's environment, tree, file and git grep output). check_skill_permissions.py fails when any rule here is missing; dispatch.settings_for merges them into every executor's settings. Add a rule here and to templates/settings.project.json together; never remove one without a decision.",
  "deny": [
    "Read(**/.env)",
    "Read(**/.env.local)",
    "Read(**/.env.production)",
    "Read(**/.env.staging)",
    "Read(**/.env.development)",
    "Read(**/.env.test)",
    "Read(**/.env.*.local)",
    "Read(**/*.env)",
    "Edit(**/.env)",
    "Edit(**/.env.*.local)",
    "Edit(**/*.env)",
    "Read(~/.ssh/**)",
    "Read(~/.aws/**)",
    "Read(~/.config/gh/**)",
    "Read(~/.npmrc)",
    "Read(~/.netrc)",
    "Read(~/.docker/**)",
    "Read(~/.git-credentials)",
    "Bash(git push --force *)",
    "Bash(git push -f *)",
    "Bash(git push *--force*)",
    "Bash(git push *--mirror*)",
    "Bash(git push *--prune*)",
    "Bash(git push *--delete*)",
    "Bash(git push -d *)",
    "Bash(git commit --no-verify *)",
    "Bash(git reset --hard *)",
    "Bash(gh pr merge *)",
    "Bash(python3 -I *graph.py* url)",
